{"slug":"traps-for-white","title":"Opening Traps for White","kind":"opening","level":"beginner","description":"Learn what an opening trap is and the golden rule for setting one. Then study three traps White can set: Légal's mate, the Fried Liver attack and Scholar's mate. For each one you also learn what Black should play to avoid it.","tags":["opening","traps","e4","white","italian-game","legal-mate","fried-liver","scholars-mate"],"reviewed":true,"chapters":[{"file":"01-golden-rule.pgn","title":"What a trap is and the golden rule"},{"file":"02-legal-mate.pgn","title":"Trap 1: Légal's mate"},{"file":"03-fried-liver.pgn","title":"Trap 2: The Fried Liver attack"},{"file":"04-scholars-mate.pgn","title":"Trap 3: Scholar's mate"}],"side":"white","chapterList":[{"id":"01-golden-rule","title":"What a trap is and the golden rule","lessons":[{"id":"what-is-a-trap","title":"What is a trap?","steps":[{"id":"01-golden-rule/what-is-a-trap/0","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"c4","to":"f7"}],"highlights":[{"color":"G","square":"f7"}],"comment":"This is a normal, healthy move. It develops a piece and eyes f7. Many traps start with moves like this."}],"hints":[],"intro":"A trap is a setup where the other player can go wrong. It only works if they make a mistake.","type":"explain"},{"id":"01-golden-rule/what-is-a-trap/1","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f1","to":"c4"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"Good. This move is sound by itself. A trap move should always be like this."}],"hints":["Use a bishop.","Move the bishop from f1 to c4."],"intro":"White to move. Play a healthy developing move that also looks at f7.","type":"find-move","side":"white"},{"id":"01-golden-rule/what-is-a-trap/2","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":[],"intro":"A trap only works when the other player goes wrong. A good opponent will not.","type":"explain"}],"teacherNotes":{"points":["A trap is a setup where the opponent can go wrong","A trap only works if the opponent makes a mistake","If the opponent plays the best move, you must still be fine","Ask the class if they have ever fallen into a trap"],"mistakes":["Thinking a trap always works","Playing a trap move that is really just bad","Forgetting that the opponent also moves"],"questions":["Does a trap work against every opponent?","What happens if the opponent sees the trap?","Have you ever fallen into a trap?"]}},{"id":"golden-rule","title":"The golden rule: stay safe","steps":[{"id":"01-golden-rule/golden-rule/0","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nd4","uci":"c6d4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2BnP3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"c6","to":"d4"},{"color":"R","from":"d4","to":"f3"}],"highlights":[{"color":"R","square":"d4"}],"comment":"The knight jumped from c6 to d4 and attacks the knight on f3."},{"san":"Nxe5","uci":"f3e5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4N3/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f3","to":"e5"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"Winning a pawn looks nice. But check the reply first."},{"san":"Qg5","uci":"d8g5","fen":"r1b1kbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4N1q1/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 5","arrows":[{"color":"R","from":"g5","to":"e5"},{"color":"R","from":"g5","to":"g2"}],"highlights":[{"color":"R","square":"e5"},{"color":"R","square":"g2"}],"comment":"Look! The queen attacks the knight on e5 and the pawn on g2 at the same time. White needs care now."}],"hints":[],"intro":"The golden rule: a trap move must also be a sound move. Always ask, what does my opponent threaten? In this lesson Black will jump a knight into d4.","type":"explain"},{"id":"01-golden-rule/golden-rule/1","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2BnP3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"Nxd4","uci":"f3d4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2BNP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f3","to":"d4"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"Safe and simple. The knight takes the knight."}],"hints":["Use your knight.","Capture the black knight on d4."],"intro":"White to move. Choose the calm, safe move that removes the jumping knight.","type":"find-move","side":"white"},{"id":"01-golden-rule/golden-rule/2","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nd4","uci":"c6d4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2BnP3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nxe5","uci":"f3e5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4N3/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qg5","uci":"d8g5","fen":"r1b1kbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4N1q1/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":[],"intro":"From g5 the queen sees along the fifth rank to e5 and down the g-file to g2. (It also eyes d2, but d2 is well guarded.) Always check what the last move attacks.","type":"explain"},{"id":"01-golden-rule/golden-rule/3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nd4","uci":"c6d4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2BnP3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nxd4","uci":"f3d4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2BNP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"exd4","uci":"e5d4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/8/2BpP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"O-O","uci":"e1g1","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/8/2BpP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQ1RK1 b kq - 1 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":["Start with the king pawn.","Develop the knight, then the bishop.","When the black knight jumps in, take it."],"intro":"Play the safe line as White.","type":"line-drill","side":"white"}],"teacherNotes":{"points":["Rule one: only set a trap with a sound move, a move that is fine even if the opponent plays the best reply","Rule two: before every move ask what the opponent threatens","Here after 3...Nd4 4.Nxe5 the black queen goes to g5 and hits both e5 and g2","A calm 4.Nxd4 exd4 5.O-O is safe","Do not say that 4.Nxe5 is bad, only that White must check the threats"],"mistakes":["Looking only at your own plan","Grabbing a pawn without checking the reply","Playing for a trap and ignoring the opponent's threats"],"questions":["What is the first question to ask before every move?","Which two things did the black queen attack on g5?","Why is 4.Nxd4 a safe choice?"]}}]},{"id":