makes a bold knight sacrifice. Watch the moves.","type":"explain"},{"id":"03-fried-liver/fried-liver/1","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n5/3np1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 6","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"Nxf7","uci":"g5f7","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2Npp/2n5/3np3/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 6","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f7","to":"d8"},{"color":"G","from":"f7","to":"h8"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The knight forks the queen and the rook, but it can be captured by the king."}],"hints":["Use the knight on g5.","Capture the pawn on f7."],"intro":"White to move. The knight on g5 can take f7. Begin the sacrifice.","type":"find-move","side":"white"},{"id":"03-fried-liver/fried-liver/2","fen":"r1bq1b1r/ppp2kpp/2n5/3np3/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 0 7","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"Qf3+","uci":"d1f3","fen":"r1bq1b1r/ppp2kpp/2n5/3np3/2B5/5Q2/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K2R b KQ - 1 7","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f3","to":"f7"},{"color":"G","from":"f3","to":"d5"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"Check, and the knight on d5 is attacked too."}],"hints":["Use your queen.","Move the queen to f3."],"intro":"White to move. The black king has come to f7. Give a check that also attacks the knight on d5.","type":"find-move","side":"white"},{"id":"03-fried-liver/fried-liver/3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Ng5","uci":"f3g5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 5 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3pp1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"exd5","uci":"e4d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3Pp1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nxd5","uci":"f6d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n5/3np1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 6","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nxf7","uci":"g5f7","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2Npp/2n5/3np3/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 6","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Kxf7","uci":"e8f7","fen":"r1bq1b1r/ppp2kpp/2n5/3np3/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 0 7","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qf3+","uci":"d1f3","fen":"r1bq1b1r/ppp2kpp/2n5/3np3/2B5/5Q2/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K2R b KQ - 1 7","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Ke6","uci":"f7e6","fen":"r1bq1b1r/ppp3pp/2n1k3/3np3/2B5/5Q2/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K2R w KQ - 2 8","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc3","uci":"b1c3","fen":"r1bq1b1r/ppp3pp/2n1k3/3np3/2B5/2N2Q2/PPPP1PPP/R1B1K2R b KQ - 3 8","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":["King pawn, knight, bishop.","The knight jumps to g5, then you take on d5.","Take f7 with the knight, then check with the queen, then develop the other knight."],"intro":"Play the Fried Liver line as White.","type":"line-drill","side":"white"}],"teacherNotes":{"points":["This is a sacrifice, not a sure win: White gives a knight for a pawn and hopes to attack the exposed king","It only appears if Black plays 5...Nxd5, which is a natural but risky move","The knight takes f7 and pulls the king out. Then Qf3+ and the bishop on c4 both attack the knight on d5, which is pinned to the king","6.d4 is a well-known strong alternative, so do not present Nxf7 as the only good move","After 7.Qf3+ Ke6 8.Nc3 White has a strong attack, but Black has more material, so White must play accurately","Do not promise a win"],"mistakes":["Playing 6.Nxf7 without checking how Black can defend","Moving the same piece again and again","Forgetting that White is down a knight until the attack succeeds"],"questions":["Which two white pieces attack f7?","Why must the black king come out to f7?","Is White ahead in material after 6...Kxf7?"]}},{"id":"fried-liver-avoid","title":"When the Fried Liver does not work","steps":[{"id":"03-fried-liver/fried-liver-avoid/0","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Ng5","uci":"f3g5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 5 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3pp1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"exd5","uci":"e4d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3Pp1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Na5","uci":"c6a5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/5n2/n2Pp1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 6","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"c6","to":"a5"},{"color":"G","from":"a5","to":"c4"}],"highlights":[{"color":"G","square":"a5"}],"comment":"The knight attacks the bishop."},{"san":"Bb5+","uci":"c4b5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/5n2/nB1Pp1N1/8/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 2 6","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"c4","to":"b5"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"White checks and keeps the bishop."},{"san":"c6","uci":"c7c6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/2p2n2/nB1Pp1N1/8/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 7","arrows":[],"highlights":[],"comment":"Black blocks."},{"san":"dxc6","uci":"d5c6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/2P2n2/nB2p1N1/8/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 7","arrows":[],"highlights":[],"comment":"White takes on c6, and Black takes back."},{"san":"bxc6","uci":"b7c6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/p4ppp/2p2n2/nB2p1N1/8/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 8","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Be2","uci":"b5e2","fen":"r1bqkb1r/p4ppp/2p2n2/n3p1N1/8/8/PPPPBPPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 1 8","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"b5","to":"e2"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The bishop retreats. White has an extra pawn, but Black has quick development."}],"hints":[],"intro":"In this lesson Black tries a calmer fifth move: 5...Na5. Instead of taking back on d5, the knight attacks the bishop on c4. Black gives up a pawn to gain time, and Nxf7 is no longer a good idea.","type":"explain"},{"id":"03-fried-liver/fried-liver-avoid/1","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Ng5","uci":"f3g5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 5 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3pp1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"exd5","uci":"e4d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3Pp1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":[],"intro":"5...Na5 does not put a knight on d5, so there is no sacrifice on f7. 5...Nxd5 is the move White hopes for.","type":"explain"},{"id":"03-fried-liver/fried-liver-avoid/2","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Ng5","uci":"f3g5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 5 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3pp1N1/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"exd5","uci":"e4d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/3Pp1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nxd5","uci":"f6d5","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2n5/3np1N1/2B5/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 6","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":[],"intro":"6.Nxf7 gives up a knight for a pawn. White gets an attack, but it needs accurate play. Never count on it.","type":"explain"}],"teacherNotes":{"points":["The Fried Liver needs Black to recapture with 5...Nxd5","The line 5...Na5 is a known good reply that moves the knight away from the bishop and gets ready for ...c6","After 6.Bb5+ c6 7.dxc6 bxc6 8.Be2 White has an extra pawn, but Black has quick development, so there is no trap and no big win","The Lichess index lists this as the Polerio Defense of the Two Knights Defense","The lesson: do not be sad when the trap does not come, just play on with the extra pawn"],"mistakes":["Expecting Black to fall for it","Sacrificing on f7 when 5...Na5 has been played","Not noticing that the black knight left the center"],"questions":["Why is 5...Na5 safer than 5...Nxd5?","Does White still have an extra pawn after 8.Be2?","What is White's plan if the trap does not work?"]}}]},{"id":"04-scholars-mate","title":"Trap 3: Scholar's mate","lessons":[{"id":"scholars-mate","title":"Scholar's mate","steps":[{"id":"04-scholars-mate/scholars-mate/0","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"c4","to":"f7"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The bishop looks at f7."},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qh5","uci":"d1h5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"h5","to":"f7"},{"color":"G","from":"h5","to":"e5"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The queen joins the attack and also hits the pawn on e5."},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f6","to":"h5"}],"highlights":[{"color":"R","square":"f7"}],"comment":"Black attacks the queen but forgets f7. This is the mistake."},{"san":"Qxf7#","uci":"h5f7","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1Qpp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"h5","to":"f7"},{"color":"G","from":"c4","to":"f7"}],"highlights":[{"color":"R","square":"e8"}],"comment":"Checkmate! The queen is protected by the bishop and the king has no square."}],"hints":[],"intro":"In this lesson the queen and the bishop will both aim at the f7 pawn. If Black ignores this, the game ends fast.","type":"explain"},{"id":"04-scholars-mate/scholars-mate/1","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 3","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"Qh5","uci":"d1h5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"h5","to":"e5"},{"color":"G","from":"h5","to":"f7"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The queen attacks the pawns on e5 and f7."}],"hints":["Use your queen.","Move the queen to h5."],"intro":"White to move. Bring the queen to a square where it attacks both f7 and e5.","type":"find-move","side":"white"},{"id":"04-scholars-mate/scholars-mate/2","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 4 4","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"Qxf7#","uci":"h5f7","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1Qpp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[{"color":"R","square":"e8"}],"comment":"Checkmate. The bishop protects the queen."}],"hints":["Use your queen.","Take the pawn on f7."],"intro":"White to move. Find the checkmate.","type":"find-move","side":"white"},{"id":"04-scholars-mate/scholars-mate/3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qh5","uci":"d1h5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qxf7#","uci":"h5f7","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1Qpp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":["Pawn, bishop, queen.","After the bishop move, bring the queen to h5.","Take on f7 and give mate."],"intro":"Play Scholar's mate as White.","type":"line-drill","side":"white"}],"teacherNotes":{"points":["The fastest well-known trap: checkmate in four moves","It only works if Black ignores the threat on f7","The queen and the bishop both aim at f7, which is guarded only by the king","Black can stop it easily, so do not rely on it","Use it to teach: protect f7 and look at what each move attacks"],"mistakes":["Playing it against everyone and learning nothing else","Not looking at what Black can do to the queen","Taking out the queen early without a plan"],"questions":["Which two white pieces attack f7?","What guards f7 for Black at the start?","Which black move on move three allows mate?"]}},{"id":"scholars-defence","title":"How Black stops Scholar's mate","steps":[{"id":"04-scholars-mate/scholars-defence/0","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qh5","uci":"d1h5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1p1p/2n3p1/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"g6","to":"h5"}],"highlights":[{"color":"R","square":"h5"}],"comment":"The pawn attacks the queen and blocks the diagonal."},{"san":"Qf3","uci":"h5f3","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1p1p/2n3p1/4p3/2B1P3/5Q2/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 1 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f3","to":"f7"},{"color":"G","from":"c4","to":"f7"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The queen steps back and still watches f7."},{"san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1p1p/2n2np1/4p3/2B1P3/5Q2/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 2 5","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"f6","to":"f7"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"Black develops. The knight blocks the f-file, so there is no mate. White's early queen move has gained nothing."}],"hints":[],"intro":"In this lesson Black answers with 3...g6. The pawn attacks the queen and blocks the diagonal to f7, so the trap fails.","type":"explain"},{"id":"04-scholars-mate/scholars-defence/1","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qh5","uci":"d1h5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":[],"intro":"3...g6 attacks the queen and blocks the h5-f7 diagonal. 3...Nf6 allows 4.Qxf7# and 3...a6 does nothing about f7.","type":"explain"}],"teacherNotes":{"points":["A simple defence is 3...g6, which attacks the queen and blocks the diagonal to f7","After 4.Qf3 the queen still eyes f7 together with the bishop, so Black must stay alert; 4...Nf6 is fine because the knight blocks the f-file","The point for White: an early queen sortie wins nothing against a careful opponent","Better habits: develop knights, castle, fight for the center","Teach Black's side too, because kids will meet this trap"],"mistakes":["Moving the queen out again and again","Forgetting to develop the knights","Ignoring that Black can attack the queen with tempo"],"questions":["Which black move attacked the queen?","Why is Nf6 fine on move four in this line but a mistake on move three?","What should White play on move three instead of Qh5?"]}}]}]}
